# Bulk Selection Fix Walkthrough

## Issue
Bulk selection (Shift+Arrow) appeared not to work because **visual feedback was missing**. The underlying logic was functional, but only the focused item showed highlighting.

## Root Cause
The `isSelected` CSS classes in [TaskItem](file:///c:/Users/mheyi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/flowstate/components/TaskList.tsx#70-281) used subtle background colors (`bg-primary-50`) that were being overridden by the `isFocused` styles due to CSS cascade order. This made it appear as if only one item was selected.

## Solution
Enhanced [TaskItem](file:///c:/Users/mheyi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/flowstate/components/TaskList.tsx#70-281) styling in [TaskList.tsx](file:///c:/Users/mheyi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/flowstate/components/TaskList.tsx#L151-160):

```diff
-${isFocused && focusMode === 'main' ? 'bg-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-800/60 ring-1 ring-slate-300 dark:ring-slate-700 shadow-lg' : ''}
-${isSelected ? 'bg-primary-50 dark:bg-primary-900/30' : ''}
+${isFocused && focusMode === 'main' && !isSelected ? 'bg-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-800/60 ring-1 ring-slate-300 dark:ring-slate-700 shadow-lg' : ''}
+${isSelected ? 'bg-primary-100 dark:bg-primary-900/40 ring-2 ring-primary-500 dark:ring-primary-400' : ''}
```

**Key changes:**
1. Focused styles no longer apply when item is selected (added `&& !isSelected`)
2. Selected items now have a prominent `ring-2 ring-primary-500` border
3. Stronger background color (`bg-primary-100`) for better visibility

